WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.431
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.731 --> 00:00:09.280
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:19.234
Unit five: Part 2: Yes/No, Choice and Indirect Answers. Today you will handle yes/no questions, either/or questions, statements and indirect replies.

4
00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:22.232
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:26.272
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:27.117 --> 00:00:28.582
Yes/no question.

7
00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:33.139
Yes/no question means a question answered with yes or no.

8
00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:34.925
Do you have a minute?

9
00:00:35.517 --> 00:00:38.448
Your turn. Say: Yes/no question.

10
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.812
Yes/no question.

11
00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:44.656
Choice question.

12
00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.905
Choice question means a question with 'or'.

13
00:00:48.517 --> 00:00:49.727
Tea or coffee?

14
00:00:50.317 --> 00:00:53.631
Your turn. Say: Choice question.

15
00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:57.770
Choice question.

16
00:00:58.517 --> 00:00:59.762
Tag question.

17
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.690
Tag question means a short question after a statement.

18
00:01:04.283 --> 00:01:05.702
You are coming, aren't you?

19
00:01:06.317 --> 00:01:09.352
Your turn. Say: Tag question.

20
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.433
Tag question.

21
00:01:14.183 --> 00:01:15.150
Statement.

22
00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.742
Statement means a sentence that gives information.

23
00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.769
I'll send the file.

24
00:01:21.383 --> 00:01:23.954
Your turn. Say: Statement.

25
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:27.836
Statement.

26
00:01:28.583 --> 00:01:29.654
Indirect.

27
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.520
Indirect means not stating the answer directly.

28
00:01:34.117 --> 00:01:36.163
An indirect answer is common.

29
00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.228
Your turn. Say: Indirect.

30
00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:42.928
Indirect.

31
00:01:43.683 --> 00:01:44.719
Suggestion.

32
00:01:45.717 --> 00:01:47.937
Suggestion means an idea about what to do.

33
00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:49.876
Why don't we meet at noon?

34
00:01:50.483 --> 00:01:53.229
Your turn. Say: Suggestion.

35
00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:57.265
Suggestion.

36
00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.041
Not sure.

37
00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.817
Not sure means uncertain.

38
00:02:02.417 --> 00:02:03.696
I'm not sure yet.

39
00:02:04.283 --> 00:02:06.785
Your turn. Say: Not sure.

40
00:02:09.633 --> 00:02:10.890
Not sure.

41
00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:12.593
Postpone.

42
00:02:13.583 --> 00:02:16.268
Postpone means to move an event to a later time.

43
00:02:16.883 --> 00:02:18.349
We postponed the meeting.

44
00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.707
Your turn. Say: Postpone.

45
00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:25.626
Postpone.

46
00:02:26.433 --> 00:02:29.782
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:33.510
Visal, what makes yes/no questions tricky?

48
00:02:34.617 --> 00:02:45.805
The answer may not start with yes or no. For example, to Did you finish the report? a correct reply may be, I'm still working on it, which means no.

49
00:02:46.917 --> 00:02:48.928
How do I answer choice questions?

50
00:02:50.017 --> 00:03:01.902
Do you want tea or coffee? is often answered with one choice, either, or neither. Listen for the exact option, such as, Coffee, please, or, Either is fine.

51
00:03:03.017 --> 00:03:05.306
What about suggestions and statements?

52
00:03:06.417 --> 00:03:17.382
To a suggestion, expect agreement, refusal or an alternative. To a statement, expect a natural comment, such as, Thanks, I'll check it now.

53
00:03:18.533 --> 00:03:20.626
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:21.483 --> 00:03:25.712
Grammar focus: Strategy: listen for meaning, not for yes or no.

55
00:03:26.012 --> 00:03:27.245
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:31.171
Did you finish the report? I'm still working on it.

57
00:03:32.083 --> 00:03:34.689
Why don't we meet at noon? That works for me.

58
00:03:35.633 --> 00:03:42.047
In Part 2 many correct answers are indirect. Think about what the reply means, and choose the one that fits naturally.

59
00:03:42.783 --> 00:03:46.457
Be careful! Don't say: I wait only for yes or no.

60
00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.167
Say: I listen for the meaning.

61
00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.420
Indirect answers exist.

62
00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:56.164
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:56.967 --> 00:03:58.444
A Natural Reply.

64
00:03:58.744 --> 00:04:01.823
Rith asks his colleague, Did you send the invoice?

65
00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:05.355
She answers, I'm waiting for the final figures.

66
00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:08.633
This means she has not sent it yet.

67
00:04:09.633 --> 00:04:12.306
Another colleague asks, Shall we meet at noon?

68
00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:16.240
He replies, That works for me, which agrees.

69
00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:21.114
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:24.672
Which reply means 'no' to 'Did you finish?'

71
00:04:24.972 --> 00:04:29.206
A, Yes, I did.. B, It's at noon.. C, I'm still working on it..

72
00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:35.637
The answer is C: I'm still working on it..

73
00:04:36.783 --> 00:04:39.201
An answer to a choice question can be blank.

74
00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:43.154
A, one choice. B, a date. C, a price.

75
00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.723
The answer is A: one choice.

76
00:04:49.883 --> 00:04:51.639
'That works for me' means blank.

77
00:04:51.939 --> 00:04:56.127
A, I do not know. B, I agree. C, I refuse.

78
00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:01.806
The answer is B: I agree.

79
00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:04.822
What is the colleague waiting for?

80
00:05:05.122 --> 00:05:09.425
A, a phone call. B, a meeting. C, final figures.

81
00:05:12.967 --> 00:05:15.570
The answer is C: final figures.

82
00:05:16.717 --> 00:05:18.380
Indirect answers are blank.

83
00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:22.078
A, common. B, rare. C, wrong always.

84
00:05:25.633 --> 00:05:27.494
The answer is A: common.

85
00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:32.200
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:35.932
Why are indirect answers common in TOEIC Part 2?

87
00:05:44.717 --> 00:05:46.182
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:46.482 --> 00:06:01.409
People often answer by explaining the situation instead of saying yes or no. For example, I'm still working on it means no. I therefore listen for the meaning of the reply rather than for yes or no.

89
00:06:01.709 --> 00:06:03.349
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:10.629
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: listen for meaning, not for yes or no.

91
00:06:10.929 --> 00:06:15.474
Today's value is critical thinking. Think carefully and give reasons for your opinions.

92
00:06:15.774 --> 00:06:18.566
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

93
00:06:18.866 --> 00:06:21.483
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

